\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 - Predictor_Coverage_Plotter_flexSDM.R
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 - PA_Map_Creator_flexSDM.R
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 - Model_Evaluation_flexSDM.R
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 - Model_Evaluation_Plots_flexSDM.R
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 - Model_Prediction_flexSDM_V2.R
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 - Spatial_Mapping_Functions_flexSDM.R
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 - Binary_Prediction_flexSDM.R
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 - Predictor_Importance_flexSDM.R
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 - Predictor_Evaluation_Strip_flexSDM.R
\par 
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 (1) creates final presence dataset per species, for each year of species surveys generates a map/raster/shapefile of where presences were observed
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45     Repeats for entire time period. 
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 (2) associates presence points with environmental information from each associated year 
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 (3) Generation of pseudo absences for each year presences were observed: generated background poin\hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 ts randomly at a rate of 20x what is needed (number of presences), perform
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45     k-means clustering (ensures environmental variability/stratification) grouping points by environmental similarity and selecting only a single point to use as a PA. 
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 (4) Cross validation: k-fold (10), Block size (GUR/RUR: 140000, PUR: 90000), repeating block assignment 200 times (to optimize spatial balance), redistribute up to 10% of presence points to folds
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45     with less than a threshold to balance folds (threshold: GUR = 80, ),\hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45  creates CAST plot
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 (5) Plot environmental and geographic coverage of the dataset, compares range of predictor data for each urchin species, build density plots comparing all variable ranges within presence points of         
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45     each data fold
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 (6) Fit an ensemble model to training data (algo: GLM, GAM, BRT, Maxent): 
\par \tab \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 BRTs: tuned with grid of hyper parameters (shrinkage: 0.05-0.0005 , n.trees: 1000-2000 , n.minobsinnode: 5-40) using AUC as a performance metric
\par \tab \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 MAXENT: tuned with grid of hyper parameters (r\hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 egmult: 0.1-5, classes: linear, linear-quadratic, linear-quadratic-hinge), using AUC as performance metric
\par \tab \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 GLM: excluded interaction terms, automated predictor selection (poly = 1, inter-order = 0)
\par \tab \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 GAM: (smoothing parameter, k=3) 
\par 
\par \tab \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 Ensembles were constructed using weighted AUC mean method (individual model predictions are weighted by their AUC values) 
\par \tab \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 Final ensemble prediction used threshold where sensitivity and specificity are equal to get binary suitability values (0-1) 
\par 
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 (7) Model Evaluation: calcu\hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 lates the testing and training AUC (how do ensemble models fit to training vs testing datasets, calculate AUC difference (AUC_training - AUC testing) and 
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45     omission error - low omission error = model does BETTER at predicting true presences, proportion of presence points in the testing dataset that are predicted below 10%, takes 
\par \tab \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 10% of predicted values of known presence points and calculates omission error as the proportion of actual presences predicted below this threshold (as unsuitable)
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45     Same metrics calculated for null models (x 1000), null model points selected randomly from environmental background
\par 
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 (8) Generate final LO predictions and uncertainty: generates rasters of LO and uncertainty, uncertainty determined by generating prediction from each model (algorithm) and determining the \tab 
standard deviation between them 
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 (9) \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 
Determine the optimal threshold for converting LO predictions to binary presence/absence: optimal threshold is determined by TSS and Omission Error, assess 1000 threshold values (between 
\par \tab \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 0-1) and assessed the optimal threshold of that 1) minimized OE and 2) maximizes TSS, builds density plot to visualize classification accuracy 
\par 
\par \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 (10) Model/Predictor interpretation: using evaluation strip method + calculate relative importance using model permutation method (100 permutations per predictor), groups predict\hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 
ors into more  \tab general classes (sums predictor importance among classes). 
\par \tab \hich\af45\dbch\af31505\loch\f45 ES method: varies one predictor at a time while holding all other predictors constant (at their mean, min and max) and then generates model predictions, gives response curves that show how LO    \tab 
